# Budget Tracker — Sheet Data Model

## Sheet Layout

The spreadsheet has **12 tabs**, one per month: `January` through `December`.

- **Row 1**: header row (skip on read/write)
- **Row 2+**: transaction data

## Column Schema (1-indexed)

| Col | Letter | Field              | Type                          | Notes                                      |
|-----|--------|--------------------|-------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| 1   | A      | `date`             | Date or M/D/YY string         | Used in duplicate-detection key            |
| 2   | B      | `business`         | string                        | Merchant name; normalized `.toUpperCase().trim()` for keys |
| 3   | C      | `amount`           | number (float)                | Stored as-is; absolute value used in keys  |
| 4   | D      | `category`         | string                        | e.g. `"Groceries"`, `"Dining"`             |
| 5   | E      | `spending_category`| string                        | Broader bucket, e.g. `"Needs"`, `"Wants"` |
| 6   | F      | `notes`            | string (optional)             | Free-text; may be empty                    |

## Transaction Object (POST payload)

```js
{
  month: "January",          // routes to the correct sheet tab
  date: "7/4/26",            // written to col A
  business: "Whole Foods",   // written to col B
  amount: 42.50,             // written to col C
  category: "Groceries",     // written to col D
  spending_category: "Needs",// written to col E
  notes: ""                  // written to col F (optional)
}
```

## Duplicate-Detection Key

```js
const key = `${dateStr}|${business.toUpperCase().trim()}|${Math.abs(amount).toFixed(2)}`;
// e.g. "7/4/26|WHOLE FOODS|42.50"
```

## Row Coloring Rules

- **Amazon rows** (`business` contains `"AMAZON"`): bg `#fff2cc`, font `#7d5a00`
- **All other rows**: inherit the existing bg/font color already used for that `category` in the sheet (looked up from `buildCategoryColorMap`)
- Category colors are keyed off **col D** (index 3); non-white, non-black backgrounds only

## GET Response Shape

```js
{
  success: true,
  existingKeys: ["7/4/26|WHOLE FOODS|42.50", ...],
  merchantHistory: {
    "WHOLE FOODS": { category: "Groceries", spending_category: "Needs" }
  },
  categoryColors: {
    "Groceries": { bg: "#d9ead3", text: null }
  }
}
```
